class.description:
The CrazyGames plugin puts a web game on CrazyGames (crazygames.com). Its SDK is loaded by the exported page (the plugin's [code]web_head[/code]), and the plugin is the [code]crazygames[/code] provider of [Services]: the game asks for its ads, game events, invite links and player there, the same calls as with any other service.
[codeblock]
async fn on_revive_pressed() {
	# CrazyGames's rewarded ad, through Services.
	if await Services.rewarded_break() {
		print("Revived")
	}
}
[/codeblock]
[Services] sends the game events by itself ([code]loadingStop[/code] when the main scene is ready, [code]gameplayStart[/code] at the player's first input, stop and start around pauses and ads), and mutes the game, ignores its input and pauses it during an ad. The plugin also follows the player's mute setting on CrazyGames ([code]muteAudio[/code]), over the game's own sound. [method Services.shareable_url] is CrazyGames's invite link, and [method Services.get_url_param] reads its parameters.
The SDK works on CrazyGames and on localhost (with test ads); on any other site it is [code]disabled[/code] and nothing happens. Outside a web game (the editor, a desktop build) the singleton is there and does nothing, and [Services] plays its test ads instead.
